# Additional model dependencies for source-checkout hardware inference.
# Install the g1_deploy package first for its Python-specific NumPy/OpenCV bounds.
# This file is not a complete lockfile.
# Install a CUDA-enabled PyTorch build appropriate for the GPU/driver separately.
# Parent training and deployment metadata use compatible NumPy bounds, but a
# successful resolution alone does not reproduce a checkpoint-tested environment.
#
# Observed CPU checkpoint-load audit, 2026-09-10:
# Python 3.12.13; torch 2.10.0+cu128; numpy 2.4.4;
# omegaconf 2.4.0.dev11; diffusers 0.38.0; loguru 0.7.3;
# scipy 1.18.0; termcolor 3.3.0; PyYAML 6.0.3.
# These observations are not a claim that an arbitrary fresh resolution or
# another CUDA/driver combination has been tested. Run bundle check --sample.
numpy
omegaconf
diffusers
loguru
scipy
termcolor
PyYAML
h5py

# Portable math/depth helpers are provided by the parent checkout's hv2_common.
# Install the parent checkout as an editable package for direct Python entry points.
#
# Real sensors additionally require platform-specific installations, maintained
# separately from this model-only list:
# - unitree_sdk2py and CycloneDDS, including G1 HG LowState/LowCmd bindings.
# - pyrealsense2 for the mounted RealSense used by the selected depth planners.
# pyrealsense2 is only needed on the USB-camera host. Network-camera inference
# uses opencv-python + pyzmq and the timestamped native depth protocol instead.
# None of these sensor dependencies are needed for bundle check --sample.
#
# Optional neural exports: onnx, onnxruntime, onnxscript. TensorRT execution also
# needs matching TensorRT 10 bindings/native libraries on the deployment host.
# Verified on Bluefin: onnxscript==0.4.0, tensorrt-cu12==10.10.0.31 with its matching
# bindings and system libnvinfer10. Do not upgrade Torch to install these extras.
